<p>This section explores each principle through practical examples.</p>
<h3 id=3D"single-responsibility-principle-srp">Single Responsibility Princi=
ple (SRP)</h3>
<p>The =E2=80=9CS=E2=80=9D in the SOLID principles stands for the Single Re=
sponsibility Principle (SRP), which states that a class should have only on=
e reason to change or, in other words, it should have a single, well-define=
d responsibility or task within a software system.</p>
<h4 id=3D"violation-of-srp">Violation of SRP</h4>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s an example of a class that violates SRP by taking on mult=
iple responsibilities:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"hljs language-java"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">class<=
